  "limitations": [
    "No live readout from an MSI MAG B650 TOMAHAWK WIFI was available.",
    "The catalog entry is ai-proposed and cannot display origin badges.",
    "The firmware exposes MSI Setup, AMD CBS and AMD AOD menus for overlapping memory settings; IFR alone does not establish which apply path wins.",
    "The MSI OC apply path in MsiOcDxe/MsiOcSmi/MsiOcMemSPDDxe/MsiOcMemSPDPei has not been fully reverse-engineered.",
    "AmdSetupRPL/AmdSetupPHX sizes and layouts differ from the DRFXI resolver fingerprint; matching offsets in some CBS timing fields do not justify reusing the DRFXI resolver.",
    "AOD RPL and PHX varstores are 0x320 bytes and differ in offsets; no AOD default NVAR entries were found, so runtime presence and attributes need a live read.",
    "CPU-family selection between RPL and PHX paths is not fully decoded; MsiOcInfoFlag exposes QuestionId 0x2C8 at offset 0x01 and QuestionId 0x2C9 at offset 0x18.",
    "The BIOS image ID E7D75AMS.1E0 is used as the exact catalog version token; confirm the actual Windows SMBIOSBIOSVersion string on the target system."
  ]
}
